	<!-- Clinical Staging Reference Information -->
	<div style="margin-top: 30px; padding: 15px; background: #f9f9f9; border: 1px solid #ddd;">
		<h3><u>Clinical Staging Key from Rwanda Breast Cancer Protocol:</u></h3>

		<h4>Early stage: fully resectable at time of presentation (operable disease)</h4>
		<ol>
			<li>Disease confined to the breast and ipsilateral axillary nodes</li>
			<li>No skin involvement (such as peau d'orange or inflammatory changes; <em>note: other overlying skin changes such as hyperpigmentation and tethering may be operable if within the mastectomy field)</em></li>
			<li>No chest wall involvement</li>
			<li>Tumor size &lt; 5 cm <em>(note: tumors &gt; 5 cm may be operable depending on size and location relative to entire breast)</em></li>
			<li>Axillary nodes not fixed to skin or underlying tissue</li>
			<li>No other lymphadenopathy</li>
		</ol>

		<h4>Locally advanced: not operable at time of presentation</h4>
		<ol>
			<li>No distant metastases</li>
			<li>No cervical lymphadenopathy or contralateral lymphadenopathy</li>
			<li>Ipsilateral supraclavicular lymphadenopathy may be considered locally advanced</li>
			<li>Localized breast skin involvement or chest wall involvement</li>
			<li>Axillary nodes fixed to skin or underlying tissue</li>
		</ol>

		<h4>Metastatic</h4>
		<ol>
			<li>Distant disease (e.g. in bones, liver, lung, brain or skin distant to breast)</li>
			<li>Cervical lymphadenopathy or any contralateral lymphadenopathy</li>
		</ol>
	</div>
